From 74d0c5443aa9e02b14dc0cacbbfc21e06dca7951 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 23:11:20 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] theme: expose Zeo design tokens through the settings
 provider

Adds the `zeo` settings namespace with its first concrete knob,
`zeo.radius_scale` (f32, default 1.0), and the `zeo_radius_scale` accessor on
ThemeSettingsProvider. Every Zeo design token resolves through this hook rather
than a compile-time constant, so a settings change reaches open windows with no
restart -- SettingsStore already refreshes on any change, so live reload needs
no new code.

The scale is clamped to 0.5-2.0 on every read, mirroring clamp_font_size. This
is a user-editable JSON file: 0 would square every corner in the app and 1000 is
a rendering pathology. A validated knob is what the settings-UI story inherits,
not a raw f32.

`zeo` is a nested top-level key, so it is a sibling group on SettingsContent
(like `title_bar`) with its own Settings impl -- ThemeSettingsContent holds the
flattened root keys and is not its home.

Covers R1.1, R1.5, R1.6, R1.7.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
